    "Ward 250 runs under a Department of Energy authorization, not a Nuclear Regulatory Commission license, and the DOE program it belongs to covers research and demonstration rather than commercial sale.",
    "Valar has also joined Texas and Utah in litigation arguing the NRC lacks licensing authority over some microreactors, according to Reuters.",
    "Alongside the demo, the two companies announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems. The concrete version under study is a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah, which Valar’s own announcement says “consumes no water from the local community.”",
