{"entry": "E17", "article": "Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says", "gold_statement": "That leaves Nvidia with \"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google", "gold_meaning": {"who": "SemiAnalysis", "what": "no proven way to expand Rubin Ultra scale-up; could give AMD and Google (whose in-house chips are winning business from top AI labs) a technical opening at the high end", "status": "forecast"}, "draws": {"A1": ["Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis", "Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \"Our roadmap is intact.\"", "\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\" the firm said", "NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.", "A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\" SemiAnalysis said.", "That leaves Nvidia with \"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\" SemiAnalysis said", "predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.", "Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.", "SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027."], "A2": ["Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap.", "Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \"Our roadmap is intact.\"", "The setback stems from difficulties manufacturing a key circuit board at the heart of the system, SemiAnalysis said in a post on Monday.", "\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\" the firm said, referring to a specialized, multi-layer printed circuit board that connects electronic modules within a system.", "NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.", "A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\" SemiAnalysis said.", "Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.", "SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027."], "A3": ["Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis", "Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \"Our roadmap is intact.\"", "\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\" the firm said", "NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.", "A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\" SemiAnalysis said.", "Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.", "SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027."], "B1": ["Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis", "Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \"Our roadmap is intact.\"", "\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\" the firm said", "NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.", "A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\" SemiAnalysis said.", "That leaves Nvidia with \"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\" SemiAnalysis said", "Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.", "SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027."], "B2": ["Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap.", "Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \"Our roadmap is intact.\"", "NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.", "A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\" SemiAnalysis said.", "That leaves Nvidia with \"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.", "Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.", "SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027."], "B3": ["Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \"Our roadmap is intact.\"", "Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap.", "\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\" the firm said, referring to a specialized, multi-layer printed circuit board that connects electronic modules within a system.", "NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.", "A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\" SemiAnalysis said.", "That leaves Nvidia with \"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.", "The delays \"should not be over analyzed as affecting the long-term criticality of Nvidia to AI data infrastructure buildouts,\" said Paul Triolo, a partner at consultancy DGA-Albright Stonebridge Group, noting the company \"has faced these kinds of challenges before, and has worked with vendors to overcome technical issues.\"", "With power supply likely to remain the major constraint on American AI data center spending, Triolo said, \"delays in getting to more advanced systems could just mean that the new systems are ready by the time the U.S. can work to overcome some of the critical bottlenecks on power now dogging the industry.\"", "Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.", "SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027."]}}
{"entry": "E29", "article": "Nvidia underperforms peers as report sparks rack delay worries", "gold_statement": "these rumored technical setbacks could severely cap the scale-up capacity of Nvidia's future hardware. This perceived vulnerability may create a wider competitive window for alternative AI platforms, specifically AMD's MI500X and Broadcom-backed custom TPUs.", "gold_meaning": {"who": "analysts cited by Bloomberg (unnamed)", "what": "setbacks could cap NVIDIA scale-up capacity and open room for AMD MI500X and Broadcom-backed TPUs", "status": "claim"}, "draws": {"A1": ["Supply chain research firm SemiAnalysis claimed in a weekend report that Nvidia's highly anticipated Kyber NVL144 rack architecture will be delayed to 2028 due to manufacturing challenges with its PCB midplane.", "An Nvidia spokesperson swiftly refuted such claims in a brief statement emailed to Investing.com, stating: \"Our roadmap is intact.\"", "The research firm further alleged that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.", "Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped."], "A2": ["Supply chain research firm SemiAnalysis claimed in a weekend report that Nvidia's highly anticipated Kyber NVL144 rack architecture will be delayed to 2028 due to manufacturing challenges with its PCB midplane.", "An Nvidia spokesperson swiftly refuted such claims in a brief statement emailed to Investing.com, stating: \"Our roadmap is intact.\"", "The research firm further alleged that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.", "Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.", "According to analysts cited by Bloomberg, these rumored technical setbacks could severely cap the scale-up capacity of Nvidia's future hardware.", "Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein dismissed such fears in his daily \"Tech Bytes\" note, calling the product delay stories \"more noise.\""], "A3": ["Supply chain research firm SemiAnalysis claimed in a weekend report that Nvidia's highly anticipated Kyber NVL144 rack architecture will be delayed to 2028 due to manufacturing challenges with its PCB midplane.", "The research firm further alleged that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.", "Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.", "According to analysts cited by Bloomberg, these rumored technical setbacks could severely cap the scale-up capacity of Nvidia's future hardware. This perceived vulnerability may create a wider competitive window for alternative AI platforms, specifically AMD's MI500X and Broadcom-backed custom TPUs."], "B1": ["Supply chain research firm SemiAnalysis claimed in a weekend report that Nvidia's highly anticipated Kyber NVL144 rack architecture will be delayed to 2028 due to manufacturing challenges with its PCB midplane.", "Our roadmap is intact.", "The research firm further alleged that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.", "Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.", "According to analysts cited by Bloomberg, these rumored technical setbacks could severely cap the scale-up capacity of Nvidia's future hardware.", "Klein noted that Hon Hai management forecasted a continued acceleration in AI demand, which the analyst said was \"a very good sign into the NVDA launch of their new Vera Rubin rack.\""], "B2": ["Supply chain research firm SemiAnalysis claimed in a weekend report that Nvidia's highly anticipated Kyber NVL144 rack architecture will be delayed to 2028 due to manufacturing challenges with its PCB midplane.", "An Nvidia spokesperson swiftly refuted such claims in a brief statement emailed to Investing.com, stating: \"Our roadmap is intact.\"", "The research firm further alleged that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.", "Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.", "According to analysts cited by Bloomberg, these rumored technical setbacks could severely cap the scale-up capacity of Nvidia's future hardware.", "Klein noted that Hon Hai management forecasted a continued acceleration in AI demand"], "B3": ["Supply chain research firm SemiAnalysis claimed in a weekend report that Nvidia's highly anticipated Kyber NVL144 rack architecture will be delayed to 2028 due to manufacturing challenges with its PCB midplane.", "An Nvidia spokesperson swiftly refuted such claims in a brief statement emailed to Investing.com, stating: \"Our roadmap is intact.\"", "The research firm further alleged that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.", "Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.", "According to analysts cited by Bloomberg, these rumored technical setbacks could severely cap the scale-up capacity of Nvidia's future hardware."]}}
{"entry": "E38", "article": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 SUPER Features A 415W TDP, 15% Higher Than RTX 5080, According to Seasonic", "gold_statement": "there are signals that NVIDIA is going ahead with the lineup instead of canceling it", "gold_meaning": {"what": "RTX 50 SUPER refresh status: earlier said to be on hold or cancelled; insider says back on track; PSU listing signals it proceeds", "period": "launch possibly late 2026 or at CES 2027", "status": "rumour"}, "draws": {"A1": ["Now further hints are landing from a PSU manufacturer who has silently added the GeForce RTX 5080 SUPER to its wattage calculator.", "Videocardz managed to find this new entry & it looks like there are signals that NVIDIA is going ahead with the lineup instead of canceling it."], "A2": [], "A3": ["For the past few months, the NVIDIA RTX 50 \"SUPER\" series was said to be essentially put on hold or outright cancelled", "there came a glimmer of hope from a well-known insider who said that the Super family is back on track .", "Videocardz managed to find this new entry & it looks like there are signals that NVIDIA is going ahead with the lineup instead of canceling it.", "Currently, there's no word on when NVIDIA will launch the RTX 50 SUPER series, and AIBs haven't started talking about these cards yet, not even at the Computex show floor, but it looks like we will get updates in the second half of this year, with a launch possibly taking place in late 2026 or at CES 2027."], "B1": ["Now further hints are landing from a PSU manufacturer who has silently added the GeForce RTX 5080 SUPER to its wattage calculator .", "So, coming to the memory specifications, it is stated that the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 SUPER will feature 24 GB of VRAM across a 256-bit bus while running at 32 Gbps, a 2 Gbps bump over the 30 Gbps used by the non-SUPER variant. These will be the latest 3 GB GDDR7 modules, and this gives us the full 1 TB/s of bandwidth, which we had hinted at a long time ago .", "Currently, there's no word on when NVIDIA will launch the RTX 50 SUPER series, and AIBs haven't started talking about these cards yet, not even at the Computex show floor, but it looks like we will get updates in the second half of this year, with a launch possibly taking place in late 2026 or at CES 2027."], "B2": ["So, coming to the memory specifications, it is stated that the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 SUPER will feature 24 GB of VRAM across a 256-bit bus while running at 32 Gbps, a 2 Gbps bump over the 30 Gbps used by the non-SUPER variant. These will be the latest 3 GB GDDR7 modules, and this gives us the full 1 TB/s of bandwidth, which we had hinted at a long time ago .", "Currently, there's no word on when NVIDIA will launch the RTX 50 SUPER series, and AIBs haven't started talking about these cards yet, not even at the Computex show floor, but it looks like we will get updates in the second half of this year, with a launch possibly taking place in late 2026 or at CES 2027."], "B3": ["Now further hints are landing from a PSU manufacturer who has silently added the GeForce RTX 5080 SUPER to its wattage calculator.", "So, coming to the memory specifications, it is stated that the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 SUPER will feature 24 GB of VRAM across a 256-bit bus while running at 32 Gbps, a 2 Gbps bump over the 30 Gbps used by the non-SUPER variant. These will be the latest 3 GB GDDR7 modules, and this gives us the full 1 TB/s of bandwidth, which we had hinted at a long time ago ."]}}
{"entry": "E41", "article": "Unannounced Nvidia RTX 50 Super GPUs appear in Seasonic PSU calculator — unreleased graphics cards shown with 10-17% higher TGP over original models", "gold_statement": "the latest sign comes from Seasonic, which has listed an RTX 5080 Super, an RTX 5070 Ti Super, and RTX 5070 Ti Super in its PSU wattage calculator", "gold_meaning": {"what": "RTX 50 Super refresh status: listed in a PSU calculator, unconfirmed by NVIDIA; trade-show talk suggests not soon", "period": "an announcement at CES 2027 or Computex 2027 'might make sense' (writer's guess)", "status": "rumour"}, "draws": {"A1": ["the latest sign comes from Seasonic, which has listed an RTX 5080 Super, an RTX 5070 Ti Super, and RTX 5070 Ti Super in its PSU wattage calculator ."], "A2": [], "A3": [], "B1": [], "B2": [], "B3": ["Seasonic gives this purported RTX 5080 Super a board power of 415W in its calculator, or 15% higher than the existing RTX 5080's 360W envelope ."]}}
{"entry": "E47", "article": "DeepSeek develops AI chips, challenging Nvidia and Huawei", "gold_statement": "DeepSeek is developing its own AI chips to reduce its reliance on products from Nvidia and Huawei", "gold_meaning": {"who": "DeepSeek", "what": "developing its own inference chips to cut reliance on NVIDIA and Huawei; early stage; talks with chip designers, foundries and memory suppliers; discreet hiring", "status": "rumour"}, "draws": {"A1": ["DeepSeek is developing its own AI chips to reduce its reliance on products from Nvidia and Huawei, which have so far been used in the development of the company's AI models.", "DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.", "Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way.", "DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology,", "adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.", "Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.", "Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.", "DeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months.", "OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, last month in collaboration with Broadcom,", "Anthropic is also reportedly considering developing its own AI chips.", "The base model supporting DeepSeek R1 was trained using Nvidia's H800 chips, a product specifically designed for the Chinese market before the US government banned its export in late 2023.", "In April, DeepSeek launched its V4 model, which had been optimised for Huawei Ascend chips, while Huawei revealed that training for the V4-Flash model also used Ascend processors.", "The launch also drove a surge in demand for Huawei's Ascend 950 chips among Chinese technology companies."], "A2": ["According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.", "Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.", "DeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months.", "\"Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology,\" said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.", "Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.", "The base model supporting DeepSeek R1 was trained using Nvidia's H800 chips, a product specifically designed for the Chinese market before the US government banned its export in late 2023.", "In April, DeepSeek launched its V4 model, which had been optimised for Huawei Ascend chips, while Huawei revealed that training for the V4-Flash model also used Ascend processors.", "At the same time, DeepSeek has begun opening itself to external funding. Reuters previously reported that the company was preparing its first funding round worth US$7 billion, with a valuation of between US$52 billion and US$59 billion, ending a years-long strategy of rejecting outside investment."], "A3": ["According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.", "Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.", "Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.", "DeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months. The hiring process has been conducted discreetly, without publicly posting job openings on general recruitment platforms.", "\"Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology,\" said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.", "The base model supporting DeepSeek R1 was trained using Nvidia's H800 chips, a product specifically designed for the Chinese market before the US government banned its export in late 2023.", "In recent months, the company has increasingly relied on Huawei's ecosystem. In April, DeepSeek launched its V4 model, which had been optimised for Huawei Ascend chips, while Huawei revealed that training for the V4-Flash model also used Ascend processors."], "B1": ["According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.", "According to Reuters sources, DeepSeek's chip development project remains at an early stage. Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors. DeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months.", "OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, last month in collaboration with Broadcom", "Anthropic is also reportedly considering developing its own AI chips.", "In April, DeepSeek launched its V4 model, which had been optimised for Huawei Ascend chips, while Huawei revealed that training for the V4-Flash model also used Ascend processors. The launch also drove a surge in demand for Huawei's Ascend 950 chips among Chinese technology companies."], "B2": ["According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.", "According to Reuters sources, DeepSeek's chip development project remains at an early stage. Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.\nDeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months. The hiring process has been conducted discreetly, without publicly posting job openings on general recruitment platforms.", "\"Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology,\" said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.", "Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.", "OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, last month in collaboration with Broadcom, while Anthropic is also reportedly considering developing its own AI chips."], "B3": ["According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.", "Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors. DeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months.", "\"Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology,\" said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.", "Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.", "In April, DeepSeek launched its V4 model, which had been optimised for Huawei Ascend chips, while Huawei revealed that training for the V4-Flash model also used Ascend processors.", "The launch also drove a surge in demand for Huawei's Ascend 950 chips among Chinese technology companies.", "OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, last month in collaboration with Broadcom, while Anthropic is also reportedly considering developing its own AI chips.", "Reuters previously reported that the company was preparing its first funding round worth US$7 billion, with a valuation of between US$52 billion and US$59 billion, ending a years-long strategy of rejecting outside investment."]}}
